                <pb facs="0234" n="140" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg140"/>

                <head>No. 104.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hall
                        to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Managua, Nicaragua</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1887-08-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 24, 1887</date>. (Received Sept. 14.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 699.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With my dispatch No. 696, of the 11th
                    instant, I had the honor to transmit an abstract of the last boundary treaty
                    between Nicaragua and Costa Rica, signed at this place on the 26th ultimo. I now
                    inclose a translation of the treaty itself.</p>
                <p>The Congress of Costa Rica is now in session, and will no doubt ratify the
                    treaty. An extra session of the Nicaraguan Congress has been called for the same
                    object, to meet on the 1st proximo. I understand that the treaty meets with
                    opposition, but the general belief is that it will be ratified.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry C. Hall.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d104-a1.xml" xpointer="d104-a1"/>
            </div>
